3. Quality‑Constrained Divergent Exploration

3.1 Geometry of the Solution Manifold

We model the space of possible outputs as a differentiable manifold \mathcal{Y} equipped with the Fisher–Rao metric derived from a parametric generative model. For a model outputting probability vectors over a vocabulary, the metric is g_{ij}(y) = \mathbb{E}_{x}[\partial_i \log p(y|x) \, \partial_j \log p(y|x)], which can be pulled back to the model’s parameter space via the mapping \phi: \Theta \to \mathcal{Y} (Yin et al., 2026). The geodesic distance d_{\text{FR}}(y_1, y_2) measures the minimal information‑theoretic path separating two outputs.

3.2 Quality‑Constrained Entropy Maximisation (QEMPO)

Let \pi_\theta be a policy parameterised by \theta. The human specifies a quality function Q: \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Y} \to [0,1] induced by verifiable constraints \mathcal{C} and a threshold Q_{\min}. The optimisation problem is

\max_\theta \; H\big(\pi_\theta(\cdot|x)\big) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad \mathbb{E}_{y \sim \pi_\theta}[Q(x,y)] \ge Q_{\min}.

The Lagrangian \mathcal{L}(\theta,\lambda) = H(\pi_\theta) + \lambda (\mathbb{E}[Q] - Q_{\min}) is maximised via policy gradient with adaptive Lagrange multiplier \lambda. Under the assumptions of (Pan et al., 2026) — Lipschitz continuity of Q and smoothness of the policy — stochastic gradient ascent converges to a stationary point of the entropy‑regularised objective, and the expected constraint violation vanishes at rate O(1/\sqrt{T}). The resultant policy achieves a Pareto‑optimal trade‑off between diversity and quality.

3.3 Geodesic Innovation Distance

For a specific output y, the innovation distance from the AI‑only centroid \mu_{\text{AI}} is

\text{Innovation}(y) = d_{\text{FR}}(y, \mu_{\text{AI}}) \cdot \text{Coherence}(y; \mathcal{C}),

where \text{Coherence}(y;\mathcal{C}) \in [0,1] is the fraction of verifiable constraints satisfied. Under the Fisher–Rao metric, if Q is L-Lipschitz in y, the product is a contraction mapping when constrained to the sub‑manifold of high‑coherence outputs, ensuring that successive refinements converge to a neighbourhood of \mu_{\text{AI}} only if innovation is genuinely absent.

